# The nine packages are tracked subdirectories of this repository (monorepo since
# 2026-10-13). The rules below that carry no leading slash apply inside them too, on
# purpose: a `data/` or `CLAUDE.md` anywhere in the tree stays out of git.

# The PRIVATE repo of site configs, dataset scripts and notebooks. configs, scripts and
# notebooks at this root are SYMLINKS into it, so they are matched below WITHOUT a
# trailing slash: `configs/` matches only a directory, and would let a symlink through.
neu-scripts-mega/

# Site configs: dask configs for one cluster's partitions, accounts and paths;
# datasets.toml, the ONE file allowed to name object-store locations, so that no committed
# doc, script or notebook has to; neu-mark.toml and its rules modules.
/configs

# Dataset-specific scripts and their records. They name real volumes and ground-truth sets.
/scripts

# Working notes and agent context. These carry ceph/S3 paths, usernames and in-flight
# run detail that do not belong in a public repository.
CLAUDE.md
notes/

# Finished plans and superseded design docs, kept for reference and named
# <repo>-<doc>-<date-last-true>. Never published, never tracked: they are records of
# what was decided and measured, and a stale design doc that looks current is worse
# than none. What is still true lives in the READMEs, the docs site and CLAUDE.md.
archive/

# neu-mark site defaults (neu_mark.config), found by walking up from the working
# directory. Personal, and it carries a server name and a branch ref.
neu-mark.toml

# Dataset content and run artefacts, which are large and belong on bulk storage, not in
# git. Note `*.log` was already here and did its job; the leak came in as `.txt`
# and `.jsonl`, so match on the NAMES, not only on extensions, and never stage with
# `git add -A` at this root.
*.log
*.progress.jsonl
data/
*-explicit-*.txt

# `environment.yml` IS tracked: it is the one spec for users and CI. These two describe
# one internal machine and stay private. `docs/requirements.txt` must stay tracked —
# the docs CI job installs from it.
/pypi_requirements.txt
/neu-vol-cv-environment.yml

# Build output and the generated pages. Generating them is the point: a committed copy
# could disagree with the code, which is the failure this site is designed to prevent.
docs/_build/
docs/_generated/
# autoapi writes the parsed API pages into the source tree and removes them again when
# the build finishes; a build that crashes partway leaves them behind.
docs/api/

# Analysis notebooks
/notebooks

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Editor state, ignored in every package repo here too.
.vscode/
.idea/
